From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:00:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: fix the GMU probe-deferral cleanup

The deferral for the GMU's "gx" power domain is hit whenever the GMU
probes before gxclkctl is ready: drm/msm is built in and gxclkctl is a
module, so a6xx_gmu_init() can get -EPROBE_DEFER, run detach_gxpd and
be retried once the module has loaded.

That cleanup path is not defer-safe:

  - it calls device_link_del() on the cxpd link. device_link_add()
    created it without DL_FLAG_STATELESS, i.e. as a managed link, and
    dropping a managed link is not allowed while its consumer is
    registered, so each deferral logged

      WARNING: Unable to drop a managed device link reference

    The link is not ours to drop anyway: dev_pm_domain_detach() just
    below unregisters the supplier (the genpd virtual device) and the
    link is purged with it, which a6xx_gmu_remove() already relies on.

  - it never undoes the pm_runtime_enable() done at the top of the
    function, so the retry logged

      platform 3d37000.gmu: Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!

    Every error path of a6xx_gmu_init() is after that enable, so undo
    it once at err_put_device.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 21b219fbfae..f9ffe6c66c3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -2497,7 +2497,10 @@ int a6xx_gmu_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(gmu->qmp))
 		qmp_put(gmu->qmp);
 
-	device_link_del(link);
+	/*
+	 * The cxpd link is a managed one and cannot be dropped while the GMU is
+	 * registered; it is purged when cxpd, a virt device, is detached below.
+	 */
 
 detach_cxpd:
 	dev_pm_domain_detach(gmu->cxpd, false);
@@ -2510,6 +2513,9 @@ int a6xx_gmu_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 err_memory:
 	a6xx_gmu_memory_free(gmu);
 err_put_device:
+	/* Every error above happens after pm_runtime_enable() */
+	pm_runtime_disable(gmu->dev);
+
 	/* Drop reference taken in of_find_device_by_node */
 	put_device(gmu->dev);
 
